Translation patch: construction of `io::Error`

Change: Every `io::Error::new(kind, x)` in the in-scope code becomes `io_error_msg(kind, "...")` (static message) or `io_error_from(kind, e)` (error value); these two new helpers in `misc/mod.rs` are just `io::Error::new(kind, x)`. They are `opaque` in Cargo.toml.
Why: `io::Error::new` takes `E: Into<Box<dyn Error + Send + Sync>>`; Aeneas does not support `dyn` types ("Dynamic trait types are not supported yet").
Behaviour: Identical: the helpers are the inlined call.

